{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41699600",
      "title": "Introducing Compound Components",
      "sourceHash": "89e5078eadcae7d51addf2625d0188b5149ec70964bba32ee110397a530aef19",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.69,
          "en": "So let's dive right in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.69,
          "end": 7.35,
          "en": "And let's start by exploring our first important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.35,
          "end": 10.38,
          "en": "slightly more advanced React pattern,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.38,
          "end": 13.59,
          "en": "the Compound Components React pattern.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.59,
          "end": 15.9,
          "en": "What is that pattern all about?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.9,
          "end": 18.675,
          "en": "What are Compound Components?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.675,
          "end": 23.049,
          "en": "Well, Compound Components are components, React components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.049,
          "end": 25.05,
          "en": "that you build such that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.05,
          "end": 27.36,
          "en": "they don't really work on their own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.36,
          "end": 32.36,
          "en": "so standalone, but instead, only together in conjunction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.12,
          "end": 35.4,
          "en": "And to understand this pattern,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.4,
          "end": 38.73,
          "en": "it helps to take a look at some default, built-in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.73,
          "end": 42.06,
          "en": "standard HTML elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.06,
          "end": 45.483,
          "en": "Outside of React, we don't have to care about React here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.41,
          "end": 51.39,
          "en": "If we consider the select and the option elements, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.39,
          "end": 54.6,
          "en": "two built-in elements built into HTML,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.6,
          "end": 59.19,
          "en": "then those elements aren't that useful on their own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.19,
          "end": 62.04,
          "en": "If you try using just the select element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.04,
          "end": 66.39,
          "en": "or just the option element, you won't achieve much.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 70.95,
          "en": "Instead, these elements are meant to be used in conjunction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.95,
          "end": 74.19,
          "en": "Then you can use the option element inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.19,
          "end": 78.48,
          "en": "of the select element to define options for a dropdown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.48,
          "end": 80.463,
          "en": "That's how these elements work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.3,
          "end": 84.09,
          "en": "And we could call them compound elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.09,
          "end": 85.35,
          "en": "or Compound Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.35,
          "end": 87.75,
          "en": "because they really only work together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.75,
          "end": 91.11,
          "en": "And it turns out that we can also build such kinds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.11,
          "end": 93.783,
          "en": "of components on our own in our React apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.783,
          "end": 98.52000000000001,
          "en": "and that in certain situations, we also might wanna do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.52000000000001,
          "end": 101.82,
          "en": "So let's explore such a situation now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.82,
          "end": 104.369,
          "en": "My first goal in this demo app here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.369,
          "end": 106.97999999999999,
          "en": "is to build an accordion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.97999999999999,
          "end": 109.709,
          "en": "So basically a section on my page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.709,
          "end": 112.05,
          "en": "where I got multiple topics",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.05,
          "end": 115.65,
          "en": "and we can click those topics to expand them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.65,
          "end": 119.03999999999999,
          "en": "The special thing about the accordion then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.03999999999999,
          "end": 121.923,
          "en": "is that as we open one of those elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.923,
          "end": 125.089,
          "en": "any other open elements close.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.089,
          "end": 129.72,
          "en": "So these elements need to know about each other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.72,
          "end": 132.789,
          "en": "so that we can control them together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.789,
          "end": 134.973,
          "en": "At the same time, I wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.973,
          "end": 138.93,
          "en": "that every element on its own is pretty independent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.93,
          "end": 141.69,
          "en": "can be styled as I need to style it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.69,
          "end": 146.19,
          "en": "and can receive any content I want to pass to that element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.19,
          "end": 148.5,
          "en": "And that's exactly what we can build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.5,
          "end": 152.07,
          "en": "by using that Compound Components pattern.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.07,
          "end": 154.89,
          "en": "Therefore, here in this project, to get started,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.89,
          "end": 158.61599999999999,
          "en": "I'll add a new components folder in the src folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.61599999999999,
          "end": 161.64,
          "en": "and in there, an Accordion folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.64,
          "end": 164.434,
          "en": "which will hold all those accordion components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.434,
          "end": 167.673,
          "en": "that are meant to be used in conjunction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.23,
          "end": 171.6,
          "en": "And here we can now start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.6,
          "end": 174.483,
          "en": "by adding an Accordion.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.483,
          "end": 177.36,
          "en": "which should hold an export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.36,
          "end": 182.36,
          "en": "and Accordion component function like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.76,
          "end": 184.95,
          "en": "And in its simple form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.95,
          "end": 186.99099999999999,
          "en": "we could say that this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.99099999999999,
          "end": 191.4,
          "en": "should deal with creating a shell for the Accordion,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.4,
          "end": 195.45,
          "en": "so a wrapper for all those Accordion items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.45,
          "end": 198.69,
          "en": "And that wrapper could be ul elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.69,
          "end": 201.093,
          "en": "since we'll output a list, essentially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.26,
          "end": 205.56,
          "en": "Then, of course, we could expect some props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.56,
          "end": 209.67000000000002,
          "en": "and use prop destructuring here to get the items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.67000000000002,
          "end": 210.87,
          "en": "that should be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.86,
          "end": 213.21,
          "en": "And then here in the list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213.21,
          "end": 215.73,
          "en": "we could map through all those items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.73,
          "end": 218.57999999999998,
          "en": "to output those list items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.57999999999998,
          "end": 220.14,
          "en": "And then we could add the logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.14,
          "end": 222.66,
          "en": "for managing those different items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.66,
          "end": 225.6,
          "en": "and for making sure that only one of those items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 225.6,
          "end": 227.25,
          "en": "is open at the same time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.25,
          "end": 229.803,
          "en": "all to that Accordion component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.76,
          "end": 233.137,
          "en": "We could do that, but if we would do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.137,
          "end": 238.137,
          "en": "it would be possible in some ways but not really convenient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 238.249,
          "end": 242.14,
          "en": "to make the individual items highly configurable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.18,
          "end": 244.89,
          "en": "so that we can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.89,
          "end": 247.83,
          "en": "control what the content of every item should be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 247.83,
          "end": 250.14,
          "en": "We would essentially hard code it all here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 250.14,
          "end": 252,
          "en": "into this one component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 252,
          "end": 255.48,
          "en": "Therefore, instead of accepting the items here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 255.48,
          "end": 259.56,
          "en": "I simply expect to get the special children prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.56,
          "end": 261.54,
          "en": "And I wanna output that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 261.54,
          "end": 265.98,
          "en": "between my unordered list tags, so that at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 265.98,
          "end": 268.53,
          "en": "this Accordion component will only create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 268.53,
          "end": 272.97,
          "en": "a shell for whatever con that we want to have in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.97,
          "end": 274.723,
          "en": "Now it will soon do more than that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.723,
          "end": 277.323,
          "en": "but for a start, it will do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278.55,
          "end": 282.54,
          "en": "In addition, I'll also expect a className prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282.54,
          "end": 284.4,
          "en": "and destructure that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 284.4,
          "end": 287.964,
          "en": "or at least I want to be able to work with such a prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 287.964,
          "end": 292.74,
          "en": "And I wanna set the class name of my ul tags here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 292.74,
          "end": 295.38,
          "en": "to the received class name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 295.38,
          "end": 297.39,
          "en": "so that it's not just a content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 297.39,
          "end": 300,
          "en": "that can be set from outside this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 300,
          "end": 304.29,
          "en": "but also the CSS class that's applied to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.29,
          "end": 306.9,
          "en": "And, of course, you could accept more props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 306.9,
          "end": 309.723,
          "en": "to make this unordered list here configurable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 310.68,
          "end": 312.6,
          "en": "With that component built here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 312.6,
          "end": 315.923,
          "en": "we can go to the App.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 315.923,
          "end": 319.05,
          "en": "And in that file here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 319.05,
          "end": 323.79,
          "en": "I want to output the main element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 323.79,
          "end": 326.793,
          "en": "and then in there, add a section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 327.84,
          "end": 330.72,
          "en": "And then for this dummy app we're building,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 330.72,
          "end": 335.15999999999997,
          "en": "add an h2 tag where I say, Why work with us?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 335.15999999999997,
          "end": 338.31,
          "en": "Because I then, below that heading, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 338.31,
          "end": 342.33299999999997,
          "en": "wanna output my accordion with some FAQ items, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 343.38,
          "end": 346.62,
          "en": "So here we can use this new Accordion component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 346.62,
          "end": 349.62,
          "en": "and import it from the Accordion.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 349.62,
          "end": 351.39300000000003,
          "en": "from the Accordion folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 352.23,
          "end": 353.94,
          "en": "And then since we built this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 353.94,
          "end": 355.86,
          "en": "in such a configurable way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 355.86,
          "end": 359.85,
          "en": "we can set the class name prop here on Accordion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 359.85,
          "end": 364.53,
          "en": "and set it to accordion because that is a CSS class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 364.53,
          "end": 367.44,
          "en": "I did prepare in the index.css file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 367.44,
          "end": 369.663,
          "en": "which was part of the starting project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 370.5,
          "end": 373.09,
          "en": "And I, of course, also wanna set the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 373.09,
          "end": 374.853,
          "en": "between those tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 375.87,
          "end": 377.4,
          "en": "And here we could, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 377.4,
          "end": 380.253,
          "en": "now add the individual list items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 380.253,
          "end": 382.442,
          "en": "but that's not really the idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 382.442,
          "end": 385.315,
          "en": "when working with Compound Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 385.315,
          "end": 389.55,
          "en": "Instead, I now wanna build more Accordion components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 389.55,
          "end": 392.275,
          "en": "that work together with that wrapper component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 392.275,
          "end": 395.4,
          "en": "so that I can output those other components here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 395.4,
          "end": 397.40999999999997,
          "en": "between those tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 397.40999999999997,
          "end": 400.347,
          "en": "Just as I explained it with the built-in select",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 400.347,
          "end": 401.97,
          "en": "and option elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 401.97,
          "end": 404.823,
          "en": "which also are meant to work together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 406.05,
          "end": 409.171,
          "en": "So let's add more Accordion-specific components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 409.171,
          "end": 413.673,
          "en": "and let's, for example, next add an AccordionItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 414.889,
          "end": 416.76,
          "en": "which, I guess, makes sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 416.76,
          "end": 420.54,
          "en": "We have the list, now we also want an item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 420.54,
          "end": 423.15,
          "en": "So in here, I'll export my component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 423.15,
          "end": 424.467,
          "en": "called AccordionItem().",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 426.69,
